      "type": "listeningPassage",
      "title": "ミニ講義",
      "note": "最初は原稿を隠し、全体の意味を聞く。次に具体情報を聞き、最後に原稿を確認する。",
      "nodes": [
        {
          "english": "ミニ講義",
          "japanese": "場面"
        },
        {
          "english": "Public transport can help reduce traffic in cities. A bus can carry many people at the same time, so fewer cars may be needed on the road. However, people are more likely to use buses when services are frequent and reliable. For example, a bus that comes every ten minutes is easier to use than one that comes once an hour. Improving public transport can therefore make daily travel more convenient.",
